  <p>Original punctuation marks are short vertical bars at median height. Some of them are more dots than bars, but since they are evidently variations of the same punctuation sign, all are represented by | in the edition. Anusvāras are dots below headline height, often as low as the median line and occasionally as low as the bottom line. Rare initial Ai occurs in line 90 and would not be distinguishable from ṣo if deprived of context. The opening symbol is a flower apparently with four petals ending in spiky points.
